# Tool sandbox

Register every domain tool in both `TOOLS` and `TOOL_FNS`. `SkillRegistry` slices those schemas by the manifest in `src/harness/skills/`. A manifest name missing from `TOOLS` fails at import. The loop sends `schemas()` for the loaded skills plus `load_skill` and `unload_skill`, not the full `TOOLS` list. `execute_tool` stays the raw sandbox; `SkillRegistry.execute` rejects a domain tool whose skill is not loaded.

Resolve every file path with `resolve_in_workspace` (`Path.resolve` plus `is_relative_to`). Reject empty paths and anything outside the workspace.

Return failures as `Error: ...` strings. `execute_tool` catches `ValueError` and `OSError`. `_tool_result` turns bad JSON into a tool error and still returns `(args_or_none, result)`.

`read_file` and `delete_file` refuse directories. `write_file` creates parents, writes UTF-8 bytes, and reports the byte count. Cap model-facing text with `cap_result` (`MAX_TOOL_RESULT`).

`run_shell` stays `shell=False`, 30s timeout, allowlisted env. Block `SHELL_META` and `DENIED_COMMANDS` (`rm`, `mv`, `chmod`, `sudo`). Reject `..` in argv parts. Check absolute args with `resolve_in_workspace`.

`fetch_url` allows only `http` and `https`, with no userinfo. Resolve the host and reject any address that is not global, and do the same on every redirect. Disable proxies. Save the body in the workspace (default `downloads/<host>-<hash>.html`) and return status, content type, byte count, and path. Cap the body at `FETCH_MAX_BYTES` and the request at `FETCH_TIMEOUT`. Accept only `text/html` and `application/xhtml+xml`.

`parse_html` reads a workspace HTML file from `path` and returns title, author, date, and article text from trafilatura. It does not download. Cap the text with `cap_result`. Missing files, directories, and empty extracts are `Error: ...`.

```python
# BAD: shell=True, or raising into the loop
subprocess.run(command, shell=True, cwd=workspace)

# GOOD: argv from prepare_shell, errors as strings
return f"Error: {exc}"
```
